  "details": "This just crossed my mind, why don't we have a feature that instead of letting us hide everyone elses avatars we hide our own from everyone?\n\nYou can turn off avatars in safety setting. Reverse it, so to speak, let me set who's even allowed to load my avatar. That'd give total control and prevent every single person in a public lobby from loading in an avatar I don't want to risk having stolen.\n\nLike setting \"Show my avatar: Friends Only\".\n\nSeems like it'd be less complicated to implement than encryption systems and whatnot. \n\nIt seems entirely in line with having a trust system and safety system to begin with that we would be able to control our own avatars visibility.\n\nThank you for your consideration",
